@page "/wiki/species"
@page "/wiki/species/{Key}"

@*
    The species classes: what a founding species can be made of, and what it can look like.

    The one shelf whose entries are a set of pictures rather than a single icon. A class is thirty
    faces or two, and which faces it can wear is most of what a reader came for - so they run full
    width under each row rather than being squeezed into a cell of it.

    The second address is one entry of the shelf. It shows the same page and picks that one out, so a
    reader who found the thing they came for can send somebody straight to it rather than to a list
    with an instruction to scroll.
*@

<PageTitle>Species - Stellaris Empire Manager</PageTitle>

<WikiSection Kind="WikiKind.Species" Focus="@Key" />

@code {
    /// <summary>The entry the address names, where it names one.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? Key { get; set; }
}
